Subject: local: allow the conformance emulator in the embedded GitHub read-only provider

NOT FOR UPSTREAM. This is a Breadboard-local substitution, recorded under
decision 3 of the Fullsend integration conformance plan.

The read-only GitHub profile that backs triage and review used to live in
fullsend-ai/agents, where agents patch 0003 added the emulator to it. Since
v0.52.0 fullsend ships it embedded in the binary
(internal/scaffold/fullsend-repo/profiles) under the reserved id
fullsend-github-ro, and a repository copy can no longer override it. So the
same two endpoints are added here, before the binary is compiled.

A provider profile is the sandbox's network allowlist. Fullsend imports
profiles verbatim and expands no variables in them, which is correct for a
policy file, so a host that varies per environment can only be added by
editing it. The posture is unchanged: read-only, enforced, and the binary
allowlist still excludes curl.

The same provider also declares GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN as a second credential
carrying the minted token, and the profile accepts it as a stored key. gh
reads that variable rather than GH_TOKEN on any host that is not github.com,
and declaring it here makes it arrive in the sandbox as a placeholder the
gateway resolves on egress, so no real token enters the sandbox. agents patch
0002 passes the non-secret GH_HOST and makes the same change to github-code.
TestScaffoldProviderCredentialsMatchProfiles pins this profile to GH_TOKEN
alone so that a scaffold copy can share a gateway with the fleet copy of the
same id; it is updated to the local shape, which is safe because the
conformance gateway only ever holds this binary's profiles.

Keep these entries in sync with agents patch 0003, which adds the same two to
profiles/fullsend-github-code.yaml for the code and fix agents.

If these profiles ever become templatable upstream, this patch should be
dropped rather than rebased.

Breadboard note: patches a file embedded at compile time, so it belongs to the
build patch list in deploy/scripts/05i-build-fullsend.sh.

diff --git a/internal/scaffold/fullsend-repo/profiles/fullsend-github-ro.yaml b/internal/scaffold/fullsend-repo/profiles/fullsend-github-ro.yaml
index 2a584694b..782692947 100644
--- a/internal/scaffold/fullsend-repo/profiles/fullsend-github-ro.yaml
+++ b/internal/scaffold/fullsend-repo/profiles/fullsend-github-ro.yaml
@@ -6,7 +6,9 @@ category: source_control
 credentials:
   - name: api_token
     description: GitHub token used by the gh CLI
-    env_vars: [GH_TOKEN]
+    # Breadboard-local: GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN is accepted as a second stored
+    # key so the github-ro provider can inject it; see providers/github-ro.yaml.
+    env_vars: [GH_TOKEN, GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN]
     required: true
 endpoints:
   - host: api.github.com
@@ -25,6 +27,33 @@ endpoints:
     protocol: rest
     access: read-only
     enforcement: enforce
+  # Breadboard-local: the conformance forge is a GitHub emulator on a cluster
+  # address, and this profile is the sandbox's network allowlist. Fullsend
+  # imports profiles verbatim and does not expand variables in them, which is
+  # correct for a policy file, so a host that varies per environment can only
+  # be added by editing it. That makes this a local substitution rather than
+  # something to send upstream.
+  #
+  # The read-only posture and the binary allowlist below are unchanged: curl
+  # stays excluded so the agent cannot make raw HTTP calls with the injected
+  # token, and these entries are enforced like the rest.
+  - host: github.local
+    port: 443
+    protocol: rest
+    access: read-only
+    enforcement: enforce
+  # github.com serves GraphQL from api.github.com/graphql. An enterprise host
+  # has no second hostname and serves it from the appliance at /api/graphql,
+  # which is the path gh posts to for any host that is not github.com. Copying
+  # the public entry's "/graphql" here allowed a path nothing asks for and
+  # denied the one that is used, so every GraphQL call the agent made was
+  # refused with policy_denied while the profile looked like it permitted them.
+  - host: github.local
+    port: 443
+    protocol: graphql
+    access: read-only
+    enforcement: enforce
+    path: "/api/graphql"
 binaries:
   - "**/gh"
   - "**/node"
diff --git a/internal/scaffold/fullsend-repo/providers/github-ro.yaml b/internal/scaffold/fullsend-repo/providers/github-ro.yaml
index 54a50b4c2..990bfa654 100644
--- a/internal/scaffold/fullsend-repo/providers/github-ro.yaml
+++ b/internal/scaffold/fullsend-repo/providers/github-ro.yaml
@@ -3,3 +3,7 @@ name: github-ro
 type: fullsend-github-ro
 credentials:
   GH_TOKEN: "${GH_TOKEN}"
+  # Breadboard-local: the same minted token under the name gh reads on any
+  # host that is not github.com. Declared here, not in env.sandbox, so the
+  # sandbox only ever sees a placeholder the gateway resolves on egress.
+  GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN: "${GH_TOKEN}"
diff --git a/internal/scaffold/provider_profile_credentials_test.go b/internal/scaffold/provider_profile_credentials_test.go
index 67741890d..732053a63 100644
--- a/internal/scaffold/provider_profile_credentials_test.go
+++ b/internal/scaffold/provider_profile_credentials_test.go
@@ -94,8 +94,17 @@ func TestScaffoldProviderCredentialsMatchProfiles(t *testing.T) {
 	// A scaffold copy that drifts from that shape cannot share a gateway with
 	// the fleet's. fullsend-github follows the same shape so that the coder
 	// role's provider and the read-only one stay interchangeable.
+	//
+	// Breadboard-local: fullsend-github-ro also accepts GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN so
+	// its provider can inject a placeholder under the name gh reads on a host
+	// that is not github.com. The conformance gateway holds only this binary's
+	// profiles, so the drift this guards against cannot arise there.
+	wantEnv := map[string][]string{
+		"fullsend-github-ro": {"GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN", "GH_TOKEN"},
+		"fullsend-github":    {"GH_TOKEN"},
+	}
 	for _, id := range []string{"fullsend-github-ro", "fullsend-github"} {
-		assert.Equal(t, []string{"GH_TOKEN"}, profileEnv[id],
+		assert.Equal(t, wantEnv[id], profileEnv[id],
 			"profile %q must declare GH_TOKEN", id)
 		assert.True(t, profileRequired[id+"/GH_TOKEN"],
 			"profile %q must mark GH_TOKEN required", id)
